Stores your tier's questions, once its cards are live: all of them in one call, as many as the tier's question target. Each is on one live card and tests what that card says: an MCQ with exactly 4 distinct options and the index of the right one, counting from 0, or free text with a reference answer and a rubric giving each level 0 to 3 as "0: ...", "1: ...". The tier has exactly one free-text question; the rest are MCQs. Code refuses a question past the target, a second free-text one, a stem that repeats another's meaning, and names every fault at once; each question that passes goes to pass 2, and goes live when it passes there.
